  "id": "instrumental-response",
  "term": "instrumental response",
  "definition": "An instrumental response is an action chosen because a person or animal has learned from its consequences which response works best for a given cue or situation. It contrasts with Pavlovian tendencies that are automatically drawn toward reward-related cues or away from punishment-related cues.",
